{
  "_comment": [
    "Hand-authored room chunks. This is the Ashfall answer to the 'hybrid'",
    "approach: the generator never invents a layout, it picks one of these",
    "authored tiles for a room whose ROLE and WIDTH fit, then the graph layer",
    "connects them and a BFS proves the result is playable.",
    "",
    "part formats, x/w are fractions of the room width:",
    "  [\"d\", x, tier, w, oneway]  deck whose TOP is tier*LevelGen.TIER (92) above",
    "                             the room slab. oneway 1 = jump up through it,",
    "                             0 = a 26 px solid slab.",
    "  [\"m\", x, tier, w, h]       solid mass whose TOP is tier*TIER above the slab,",
    "                             hanging DOWN h px. Fractional tiers are legal",
    "                             (a 1.5 tier wall is 138 px).",
    "Every template is authored to be self-contained: each surface is within one",
    "TIER (92 px) of the surface it is climbed from, and every surface TOP is at",
    "least LevelGen.BODY_HEADROOM (72 px) above any other surface top it overlaps.",
    "Note the guard compares tops, so a 26 px mass one tier up leaves 66 px of",
    "real air - the case LevelGen.SPAWN_LIFT is tuned against."
  ],
